CPBM  outline(color)

The CSS Box Model is a fundamental concept in web design that describes how every HTML element is represented as a rectangular box, and how its size and spacing are calculated.

Each box consists of four layers (from inside out):

Content – The actual text, image, or other media inside the element.
Padding – Space between the content and the element’s border.
Border – The line surrounding the padding and content.
Margin – Space outside the border, separating the element from others.



